{"t": "n", "id": "sec-zzh7de33", "rev": 1, "kind": "section", "key": null, "title": "2026-11-03 — A chunk's own evidence file fails `rec.py check` until it is landed", "body": null, "data": {"head": "## 2026-11-03 — A chunk's own evidence file fails `rec.py check` until it is landed\n", "level": 2, "region": "frame", "fam": "harness"}}
{"t": "n", "id": "fct-zntbl2yj", "rev": 1, "kind": "fact", "key": null, "title": null, "body": "`rec.py check` counts every regular file in a pending chunk's working folder that has not been landed as a failure\n(`records: docs · unlanded {n}`, then `check: {n} failure(s)`), even when every other store reading is clean. So a plan\nstep that writes evidence into the working folder and a later step that asserts `check: clean` need a land between\nthem: `gate.py hygiene` first, then `rec.py land --chunk {marker}`, the same pair implement fires at its end. A second\nland later keeps an unchanged file at its rev. The operator ruled this land the tool's own step, not a workaround.\n\n", "data": {"fam": "harness"}}
